 x < -300:\n        player.change(LedSpriteProperty.X, -1)\n    elif x > 300:\n        player.change(LedSpriteProperty.X, 1)\n    basic.pause(300)\n    drop.change(LedSpriteProperty.Y, 1)\n    if drop.is_touching(player):\n        game.game_over()\n    elif drop.get(LedSpriteProperty.Y) == 4:\n        game.add_score(1)\n        drop.set(LedSpriteProperty.Y, 0)\n        drop.set(LedSpriteProperty.X, randint(0, 4))","new":[11,12,13],"what":"<p><code>drop.is_touching(player)</code> is True when the two sprites are on the same LED. <code>game.game_over()</code> ends the game and shows your score. We check for a hit first, then check for a dodge.</p>","tip":"","stuck":[],"test":["Getting hit ends the game","My score shows after the game ends","Dodging still adds points"],"ask":"What is your high score? What is your partner's?","fields":[],"picture":null,"wiring":[]},{"part":"Part 2: Build the game","title":"Checkpoint: the whole game","say":"<p>Your program should match this. Compare it line by line, especially the indentation.</p>","do":[],"code":"player = game.create_sprite(2, 4)\ndrop = game.create_sprite(randint(0, 4), 0)\nwhile not game.is_game_over():\n    x = input.acceleration(Dimension.X)\n    if x < -300:\n        player.change(LedSpriteProperty.X, -1)\n    elif x > 300:\n        player.change(LedSpriteProperty.X, 1)\n    basic.pause(300)\n    drop.change(LedSpriteProperty.Y, 1)\n    if drop.is_touching(player):\n        game.game_over()\n    elif drop.get(LedSpriteProperty.Y) == 4:\n        game.add_score(1)\n        drop.set(LedSpriteProperty.Y, 0)\n        drop.set(LedSpriteProperty.X, randint(0, 4))","new":[],"what":"","tip":"","stuck":["<strong>Indentation:</strong> lines inside the loop are pushed in once; lines inside <code>if</code> / <code>elif</code> are pushed in twice.","<strong>Capital X and Y</strong> after <code>LedSpriteProperty</code>, lowercase <code>x</code> for your tilt number.","<strong>Two equals signs</strong> in <code>== 4</code>."],"te